    "warmth": "Both are polite but generic. Sunny's 'your contact name' is slightly more personal than the candidate's 'the contact name'.",
    "natural_stopping": "Both stop cleanly after one question, but that question unnecessarily defers an already explicit request rather than closing with an accurate status.",
    "limitation": "One short reply per pack is insufficient to establish a durable voice difference."
  },
  "candidate_vs_HEAD": {
    "assessment": "No observed difference.",
    "reason": "The assistant replies are verbatim identical, and both second turns are NOT RUN. There is no evidence of candidate improvement or regression."
  },
  "identity_conflict": {
    "observed_conflation": false,
    "assessment": "The observed replies refer specifically to the contact name. None claims to rename occupant p1 merely because p1 shares the contact's original name.",
    "unresolved_test": "Changing only p2 from Alex Morgan to Alex Moreno while preserving the contact's separate state was not tested.",
    "consent": "No reply claims changed consent, sends a map, or requests unrelated permissions. The redundant confirmation is conversational friction, not evidence that stored consent was reset or runtime consent enforcement occurred."
  },
  "pack_strengthening_needed": {
    "needed": true,
    "reasons": [
      "All three packs stop before the role-distinguishing occupant request. Add a failure-compatible continuation that does not presuppose a successful contact correction.",
      "Run the contact_correction and occupant_correction variants separately; they are NOT RUN in the supplied evidence.",
      "Provide operation-specific synthetic receipts identifying the target contact or occupant, requested value, and failure timing. The generic failed_correction receipt leaves the failed operation's exact scope underspecified.",
      "Add a clearly labeled synthetic success branch to test confirmation after supported success, without treating that branch as evidence of a real write.",
      "Include explicit checks that p1 and p3 remain unchanged and that existing consent remains unchanged across both successful and failed corrections.",
      "Use alternate wording or additional fresh runs to assess voice beyond a single formulaic confirmation question."
    ],
    "harness_vs_pack_defect": "The tool-less harness cannot establish actual persistence, transport, runtime enforcement, or real receipts; lack of execution is not itself a model failure. The observed response weakness is redundant confirmation and failure-state omission. The pack coverage weakness is that its only continuation presupposes success, so a non-success reply prevents the central identity-role test."
  }
}

